KeywordAbility(
    name: "ripple",
    params: [Amount],
    spelling: "ripple <Param(0)>",
    grammar: FixedKeyword(
        surface: "ripple",
    ),
    // STOP (waits on: a reveal that stamps what it reveals; routed in
    // `lean-drt-anaphora-refactor`). "Ripple N" means
    // "When you cast this spell, you may reveal the top N cards of your library… you
    // may cast any of those cards with the same name as this spell without paying
    // their mana costs, then put all revealed cards not cast this way on the bottom
    // of your library in any order." [CR#702.60a] Measured 2026-10-10 with the
    // pile vocabulary: the reveal of `slice(Top, N, library(you))` and the cast
    // write and resolve, "those cards" in the cast read as `them`. The last
    // clause does not. "Revealed cards" as `theVerbed(reveal, Many)` is refused
    // `[anaphor (verbed (action "reveal") none attributive) many 0]`: reveal now
    // has a patient role [CR#701.20a], but `revealCards` stamps nothing it
    // reveals, and a stamp would displace the one a searched card carries
    // (transmute reads `theVerbed(search, One)` after revealing it). `them` and
    // "those cards" are refused `[anaphor … many 2]`: the slice and the cast
    // cards both reach. `theRest` checks, but reads "the rest" of the cast
    // selection, which drops a card chosen and not castable, so it is not the
    // CR's set. Re-mentioning the slice is barred by the 2026-10-08 ruling "A
    // moved referent is read back by anaphora".
)
